concept.execution_logic:
SOLUTION: Phase 2: Patched WebrtcVideoCodecFactory.cpp to gate software VP8/VP9/AV1 decoder/encoder creation behind media.gorilla.hardware_only_mode preference. Patched VideoConduit.cpp to disable AV1 capability reporting. Phase 3: Patched WebCodecsUtils.cpp to restrict IsSupportedVideoCodec to H.264 only. Patched MediaCapabilities.cpp to report VP8/VP9/AV1 as unsupported in CheckCodecSupport. Patched VideoDecoder.cpp and VideoEncoder.cpp Validate() methods to reject non-H.264 codec configurations early. Updated deploy.sh with 6 new file mappings. Cleaned up 8 unmodified audit-only baseline files (AudioConduit.cpp, CodecInfo.cpp, PeerConnectionImpl.cpp, DecoderTemplate.cpp, MediaCapabilitiesValidation.cpp, TextureClient.cpp, ImageContainer.cpp, DMABufSurface.cpp) per the Cleanup of Unmodified Files directive.

Phase 2 WebRTC Gating: WebrtcVideoCodecFactory.cpp - added StaticPrefs::media_gorilla_hardware_only_mode() checks to SupportsDecoder, SupportsEncoder, CreateDecoder, CreateEncoder for VP8/VP9/AV1 case branches. VideoConduit.cpp - overrode HasAv1() to return false when hardware-only mode is active. Phase 3 WebCodecs Gating: WebCodecsUtils.cpp - inserted early return in IsSupportedVideoCodec() to accept only H.264 codec strings. MediaCapabilities.cpp - added pre-check in both decode and encode CheckCodecSupport() overloads to return CodecSupport::Unsupported for non-H.264 video MIME types. VideoDecoder.cpp - added #include mozilla/StaticPrefs_media.h and GORILLA PATCH block in VideoDecoderTraits::Validate() after codec string parsing to reject VP8/VP9/AV1 via IsSupportedVideoCodec(). VideoEncoder.cpp - identical pattern in VideoEncoderTraits::Validate(). deploy.sh updated with 6 new deploy_file entries mapping Phase 2 and Phase 3 .cpp files to their target paths under firefox-main/dom/media/.

CODE:
